.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt DROPBEAR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dropbear ,
.Nm dbclient ,
.Nm dropbearkey ,
.Nm dropbearmulti
.Nd SSH server, client, and key generator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm dropbearmulti
.Cm dropbear
.Op Ar server_options
.Nm dropbearmulti
.Cm dbclient
.Op Ar client_options
.Ar host
.Op Ar command
.Nm dropbearmulti
.Cm dropbearkey
.Fl t Ar type
.Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar bits
.Nm dropbearmulti
.Cm dropbearkey
.Fl y
.Fl f Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Rach2 installs Dropbear 2022.83 as one static executable,
.Pa /bin/dropbearmulti .
Its first argument selects the SSH server
.Cm dropbear ,
the client
.Cm dbclient ,
or the key generator
.Cm dropbearkey .
The images install only the multi-call name; invoke the client as
.Ql dropbearmulti dbclient HOST .
.Pp
The build supports Curve25519, ECDH, ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-128 and
AES-256 in CTR mode, Ed25519, public-key authentication, and password
authentication.
It has no zlib compression, syslog, utmp, wtmp, lastlog, or login message
of the day.
The executable is not position-independent.
.Pp
Init-metal starts the server at boot and supervises it; recovery's init
does so only when
.Pa /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
is a readable file with a line that is neither blank nor a comment.
They use
.Fl g
to disable root password logins unless
.Xr sshd.conf 5
permits them.
Interactive logins have separate pseudo-terminals; see
.Xr console 4 .
On a RAM root, missing host keys are generated with
.Fl R .
An installed root keeps its host keys.
The public keys authorized for an account are in
.Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys .
Recovery accepts the key it was built with, and starts no server without
one.
.Pp
There is no sftp server, so
.Nm scp
does not work.
From the host, send a file with:
.Dl ssh HOST 'cat > FILE' < FILE
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Shared server and client options
These options apply to
.Cm dropbear
and
.Cm dbclient .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl W Ar bytes
Set the receive window buffer size for each channel.
A larger window uses more memory and may improve network performance.
Use
.Fl h
to display the default.
.It Fl K Ar seconds
Send keepalive traffic at the given interval.
Zero disables keepalives.
Close the connection after three consecutive keepalives receive no response.
.It Fl I Ar seconds
Disconnect after this many seconds without transmitted or received traffic.
.It Fl z
Disable the requests for quality-of-service marking, which Rach2 accepts
and ignores.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Ss Server options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar banner
Display the contents of
.Ar banner
before login.
No banner is displayed by default.
.It Fl r Ar hostkey
Read the host key from
.Ar hostkey .
The file is generated by
.Cm dropbearkey .
When this option is given, the default host-key files are not loaded.
.It Fl R
Generate missing host keys in the default location when the first
connection is established.
.It Fl F
Stay in the foreground.
.It Fl e
Pass the server's environment to child processes.
The environment is not passed by default.
Passing it can expose secrets from the calling process.
.It Fl w
Disallow root logins.
.It Fl s
Disable password logins.
.It Fl g
Disable password logins for root.
.It Fl t
Require both public-key and password authentication.
Do not combine with
.Fl s .
.It Fl j
Disable local port forwarding.
.It Fl k
Disable remote port forwarding.
.It Fl p Ar [address:]port
Listen on the given address and TCP port.
If only a port is given, listen on all addresses.
Up to ten listening addresses may be specified.
The default port is 22.
.It Fl i
Run as a service under a TCP server such as inetd.
This implies
.Fl F
and ignores
.Fl p .
.It Fl P Ar pidfile
Write the daemon's process ID to
.Ar pidfile .
The default is
.Pa /var/run/dropbear.pid .
.It Fl a
Allow remote hosts to connect to forwarded ports.
.It Fl T Ar attempts
Set the maximum number of authentication attempts per connection.
The default is ten.
.It Fl c Ar command
Run
.Ar command
instead of the command requested by the user.
This overrides a
.Ql command=
restriction in
.Pa authorized_keys .
The original command is saved in
.Ev SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND .
.El
.Ss Client options
.Ar host
may be written as
.Ar user@host
to select the login name, or as
.Ar host^port
to select the port.
An optional
.Ar command
is run on the remote host, normally through the user's shell.
Without a command, the client opens an interactive session.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar port
Connect to the remote TCP port.
The default is 22.
.It Fl i Ar idfile
Read an identity key from
.Ar idfile .
May be repeated.
The default is
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_dropbear .
.It Fl L Ar [listenaddress:]listenport:host:port
Forward the local listening port through the SSH connection to
.Ar host:port .
.It Fl R Ar [listenaddress:]listenport:host:port
Forward the remote listening port through the SSH connection to
.Ar host:port .
.It Fl l Ar user
Log in as
.Ar user .
.It Fl t
Allocate a pseudo-terminal.
This is the default without a remote command.
.It Fl T
Do not allocate a pseudo-terminal.
This is the default with a remote command.
.It Fl N
Request no remote shell and run no command.
Command arguments are ignored.
.It Fl f
Fork into the background after authentication.
A command or
.Fl N
is required.
.It Fl g
Allow non-local hosts to connect to ports forwarded with
.Fl L
or
.Fl R .
The server may further restrict remote connections to
.Fl R
ports.
.It Fl y
Accept unknown host keys.
A mismatch with a known host key still aborts the connection.
Given twice, this option disables all host-key checking.
.It Fl A
Forward authentication-agent connections to the remote host.
Agent authentication and forwarding do not work on Rach2, which refuses
the Unix domain socket the agent is reached through.
The client can use an OpenSSH-style agent through
.Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
for public-key authentication without forwarding it.
Forwarding lets the remote server use the agent's authentication credentials.
.It Fl J Ar proxy_command
Use a proxy command's standard input and output instead of a TCP connection.
The command runs through the default shell.
A host name is still required for host-key checking.
An argument of the form
.Ql &fd
uses the numeric file descriptor as a socket instead.
.It Fl B Ar endhost:endport
Connect through the SSH host to
.Ar endhost:endport
and use the forwarded connection as the client's standard input and output.
.It Fl c Ar cipherlist
Enable the comma-separated list of ciphers.
Use
.Fl c Cm help
to list the choices.
.It Fl m Ar MAClist
Enable the comma-separated list of message authentication codes.
Use
.Fl m Cm help
to list the choices.
.It Fl o Ar option
Set an option in OpenSSH configuration format.
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width DisableTrivialAuth
.It Cm ExitOnForwardFailure
Exit if any requested local or remote port forwarding cannot be established.
The value is
.Ql yes
or
.Ql no ;
the default is
.Ql no .
.It Cm Port
Set the remote port, as with
.Fl p .
.It Cm DisableTrivialAuth
Reject authentication success without a password or public-key prompt.
.El
.It Fl s
Request the command as a subsystem.
.It Fl b Ar [address][:port]
Bind the connection to the given local address, port, or both.
.El
.Ss Key-generator options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t Ar type
Generate a key of type
.Ql rsa ,
.Ql ecdsa ,
or
.Ql ed25519 .
.It Fl f Ar file
Write the private key to
.Ar file ,
or read it with
.Fl y .
.It Fl s Ar bits
Set the key size in bits.
.It Fl y
Print the public key and fingerprint of the private key in
.Ar file .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
.It Pa /bin/dropbearmulti
Static multi-call executable.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
Public keys authorized to log in to the account.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_dropbear
Default client identity file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Connect from the host:
.Dl ssh -i krffs/rach2_demo_ed25519 root@ADDRESS
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run ssh
and
.Ql tests/run metal
exercise SSH logins.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr console 4 ,
.Xr sshd.conf 5 ,
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh HISTORY
